From: Sami <247917809+0c33@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 04:33:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(gfx906): keep the drafter's sliding window in the
 non-causal FA path

FA-NONCAUSAL stage 1 zeroed `window` for non-causal batches, so a DFlash2
drafter (all layers sliding 2048, is_causal false) attended over
[0, seq_len). The KV-cache manager frees a sliding layer's blocks once they
fall out of the window, so beyond ~2k context the drafter read freed blocks
and acceptance dropped to exactly 0 %: on main + the fp16 fix, 9.6 t/s at a
4.6k-token prompt (1.00 tokens/step); with this fix 34.8 t/s (3.66), and
3.70 / 3.85 tokens/step at 14.6k / 24.4k.

Keep the window for the gather clip and express "no causal clip, left
window only" with the kernel's existing mask: q_abs_offset = seq_len puts
every key before the row, and widening the window by the block length lands
the window test on each row's true position. No kernel change; the gather
clip and k-loop start are the ones causal sliding layers already use.

Test: a non-causal block over a 512-token context whose out-of-window
blocks point at a NaN block must match the windowed reference (fails on the
previous code with "read a freed block outside the window").

